  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID Improved Basic Education in the Kyrgyz Republic, Okuu Keremet!</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Kyrgyz Republic):  .USAID invests in the economic and political future of the Kyrgyz Republic by improving education for its youngest citizens. Planned support will give children a better foundation for educational achievement by improving instructional quality in both math and reading through improved curricula and stronger teacher training, mentorship, and support systems. To improve the learning environment, the activity will increase community support for learning, conduct out-of-school learning activities, and increase the availability of learning materials through development, production, and distribution. Lastly, programming will improve the capacity of the Ministry of Education and Sciences, by providing technical support to optimize the education system for greater efficiencies, improve pre-service training for teachers and education leaders, and increase access to quality education for all students, especially vulnerable populations...This activity supports the ICS Mission Objective 3.2: Government institutions that can effectively formulate and implement policies and provide quality services in an equitable and transparent, accountable way. Okuu Keremet(!) contributes $3,645,0002 towards Operating Unit Basic Education directive through this mechanism; $200,000 are contributed from Administration and Oversight and $20,000 from Program Design and Learning... ...</narrative>
  </description>
